ng_l2cap: take an unrequested LP_ConnectCfm as an open ACL link

ng_l2cap knew only the ACL links it asked ng_hci for (LP_ConnectReq) or
accepted (LP_ConnectInd). bluetoothd creates its links itself through
ng_hci's RAW hook, and ng_l2cap learned of such a link only when
something first opened a channel on it; the remote side's signalling and
the Encryption Change that came before were dropped as being for an
unknown handle, and Beats Studio Pro then stall every channel (see
NgHCI's 0012, which now sends LP_ConnectCfm for these links).

On a positive LP_ConnectCfm for an ACL link we have no descriptor for,
make one in the open state with that handle. It is not ours, so it gets
no CON_OUTGOING and no auto-disconnect timeout, like an accepted link.
A handle already in use is refused.

Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd#666). Not upstream.
Applies to: releng/15.1 sys/netgraph/bluetooth/l2cap/ng_l2cap_llpi.c,
after 0003.

--- a/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/l2cap/ng_l2cap_llpi.c
+++ b/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/l2cap/ng_l2cap_llpi.c
@@ -158,6 +158,37 @@
 	ep = (ng_hci_lp_con_cfm_ep *) (msg->data);
 	/* Check if we have requested/accepted this connection */
 	con = ng_l2cap_con_by_addr(l2cap, &ep->bdaddr, ep->link_type);
+	if (con == NULL && ep->status == 0 &&
+	    ep->link_type == NG_HCI_LINK_ACL) {
+		/*
+		 * NextBSD: an ACL link we neither requested nor accepted,
+		 * created through ng_hci's RAW hook (bluetoothd sends
+		 * Create_Connection itself). ng_hci tells us as soon as it is
+		 * up, so the remote side's signalling and the Encryption
+		 * Change that may follow at once are not dropped as being for
+		 * an unknown handle (nextbsd/nextbsd#666). Take it as open; it
+		 * is not ours, so no auto disconnect (no CON_OUTGOING).
+		 */
+		if (ng_l2cap_con_by_handle(l2cap, ep->con_handle) != NULL) {
+			NG_L2CAP_ALERT(
+"%s: %s - unexpected LP_ConnectCfm event. " \
+"Connection handle already in use, con_handle=%d\n",
+				__func__, NG_NODE_NAME(l2cap->node),
+				ep->con_handle);
+			error = EEXIST;
+			goto out;
+		}
+
+		con = ng_l2cap_new_con(l2cap, &ep->bdaddr, ep->link_type);
+		if (con == NULL) {
+			error = ENOMEM;
+			goto out;
+		}
+
+		con->state = NG_L2CAP_CON_OPEN;
+		con->con_handle = ep->con_handle;
+		goto out;
+	}
 	if (con == NULL) {
 		NG_L2CAP_ERR(
 "%s: %s - unexpected LP_ConnectCfm event. Connection does not exist\n",
